                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 43.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received July 19, 1870.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. W. Hoffman to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-18"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >July</hi> 18, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Consented to take North German under protection, on application of ambassador,
                    with assent of France. No answer as regards steamers.</p>
                <p>Washburne returns immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HOFFMAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Paris.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
